# Omen Alpha — exclusion notes by GPT-6 Luna

- Source: Omen Alpha exact-ID benchmark and public-catalog review
- Date: 2026-11-02 (UTC)

## Findings and exclusion rationale

- OpenCode announced Omen Alpha as a stealth model for Go subscribers on 2026-09-04. A separate evaluator reports testing the exact `omen-alpha` ID through `https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1`; this establishes a model-specific route at evaluation time, but not the underlying developer or lineage.
- The evaluator reports a custom `llmbench` coding run on 2026-09-04: 60 tasks × 5 trials, Resolved 95.0% (57/60), average success 95.7%, Quality 84.5, Combined 88.3; on a separate 16-task L7 set × 3 trials, 13/16 resolved (81.2%). The public MIT harness is available for inspection.
- Treat these as exact-ID, self-reported coding results, not as an official vendor benchmark or an independently replicated leaderboard score. The suite is evaluator-authored and non-standard; the author notes the 60-task set saturates on 40 easy-through-frontier tasks, and flags two L7 items (t103/t105) as likely benchmark-specification defects. No independent rerun was found. The separate `omenalpha.io` 23.14/40 claim is not corroborated and is not used.
- The results support a qualitative conclusion that this route performed well on that coding suite, but do not provide a defensible normalized score under the project's listed coding benchmarks. More importantly, no exact-model evidence was found for Tool use, general Reasoning, Context window, or Multimodal capability. The current OpenCode Data record (2026-10-29) lists lab as unknown, no model specifications, and `benchmarks: []`; current OpenCode Go documentation does not list Omen Alpha. No current exact-model token pricing was verified. Assigning the required full scorecard would therefore require unsupported values for most dimensions.
- No normalized scores are assigned and no GLM/Ox Alpha results are transferred. Retain this entry as excluded pending attributable evidence sufficient for a complete scorecard (or a documented project policy for coding-only ratings); this is no longer a zero-benchmark exclusion.

